2026-10-28T17:47:50.8664765Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016RmcY6rQ89f7uMJuaQfW1p","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"number\": 36,\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/36\",\n  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n  \"title\": \"[Bug]: aws_bedrockagentcore_harness produces inconsistent result after apply for memory.agentcore_memory_configuration.retrieval_config\",\n  \"body\": \"### Terraform Core Version\\n\\n1.12.6 (OpenTofu)\\n\\n### AWS Provider Version\\n\\n6.65.0\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s)\\n\\n- aws_bedrockagentcore_harness\\n\\n### Expected Behaviour\\n\\n`terraform apply` (or `tofu apply`) completes successfully when creating an `aws_bedrockagentcore_harness` with a `memory` block that does not configure `retrieval_config` under `agentcore_memory_configuration`.\\n\\n### Actual Behaviour\\n\\nApply fails with a provider consistency error because the service populates `retrieval_config` server-side even though it was not set in configuration, and the schema does not model it as Computed:\\n\\n```\\nError: Provider produced inconsistent result after apply\\n\\nWhen applying changes to module.harness.aws_bedrockagentcore_harness.this, provider\\n\\\"provider[\\\\\\\"registry.opentofu.org/hashicorp/aws\\\\\\\"]\\\" produced an unexpected new value:\\n.memory[0].agentcore_memory_configuration[0].retrieval_config: block count changed\\nfrom 0 to 1.\\n\\nThis is a bug in the provider, which should be reported in the provider's own issue tracker.\\n```\\n\\nThis is the same class of bug as `#48159` / PR `#48815`, where AWS-populated fields under `aws_bedrockagentcore_harness` were not marked Computed in the schema, causing the post-apply consistency check to fail. That fix covered `environment.agentcore_runtime_environment`; this issue is the same problem for `memory[0].agentcore_memory_configuration[0].retrieval_config`.\\n\\n### Relevant Error/Panic Output Snippet\\n\\n```\\nError: Provider produced inconsistent result after apply\\n\\nWhen applying changes to module.harness.aws_bedrockagentcore_harness.this, provider\\n\\\"provider[\\\\\\\"registry.opentofu.org/hashicorp/aws\\\\\\\"]\\\" produced an unexpected new value:\\n.memory[0].agentcore_memory_configuration[0].retrieval_config: block count changed\\nfrom 0 to 1.\\n\\nThis is a bug in the provider, which should be reported in the provider's own issue tracker.\\n```\\n\\n### Terraform Configuration Files\\n\\n```hcl\\nresource \\\"aws_bedrockagentcore_harness\\\" \\\"this\\\" {\\n  harness_name       = \\\"${var.project_name}_${var.environment}_${var.harness_name}\\\"\\n  execution_role_arn = aws_iam_role.harness.arn\\n  region              = var.aws_region\\n\\n  system_prompt {\\n    text = var.system_prompt_text\\n  }\\n\\n  model {\\n    bedrock_model_config {\\n      model_id = var.harness_model_id\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  memory {\\n    agentcore_memory_configuration {\\n      arn            = var.memory_arn\\n      actor_id       = var.actor_id\\n      messages_count = var.messages_count\\n      # retrieval_config intentionally not set\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Steps to Reproduce\\n\\n1. Create an `aws_bedrockagentcore_harness` resource with a `memory` block configuring `agentcore_memory_configuration` (arn, actor_id, messages_count) but without a `retrieval_config` block.\\n2. Run `terraform apply`.\\n3. The apply succeeds in creating the resource on the AWS side, but Terraform's post-apply consistency check fails because the API response includes a `retrieval_config` block that was not present in the planned configuration.\\n\\n### Debug Output\\n\\n_Can provide on request \\u2014 redacting account-specific details first._\\n\\n### Panic Output\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Important Factoids\\n\\nLikely the same root cause as `#48159` (service-populated/computed fields under `aws_bedrockagentcore_harness` not marked `Computed` in the schema). The fix in PR `#48815` addressed `environment.agentcore_runtime_environment`; `memory[0].agentcore_memory_configuration[0].retrieval_config` appears to need the same treatment.\\n\\n### References\\n\\n- `#48159`\\n- `#48815`\\n- `#50056`\\n\\n\",\n  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"labels\": [],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:10:00Z\",\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-21T09:55:24Z\"\n}{\n  \"decision\": null,\n  \"labels\": [],\n  \"comment\": null,\n  \"duplicate_of\": [],\n  \"reason\": null\n}{\n  \"issue\": {\n    \"number\": 36,\n    \"title\": \"[Bug]: aws_bedrockagentcore_harness produces inconsistent result after apply for memory.agentcore_memory_configuration.retrieval_config\",\n    \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n    \"labels_at_open\": []\n  },\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-21T09:55:24+00:00\",\n  \"form\": {\n    \"template\": null,\n    \"missing_required\": [],\n    \"empty_optional\": [],\n    \"used_form\": false\n  },\n  \"services\": {\n    \"resources_mentioned\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"aws_bedrockagentcore_harness\",\n        \"resource_exists\": true,\n        \"data_source_exists\": false,\n        \"service_label\": \"service/bedrockagentcore\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"aws_iam_role\",\n        \"resource_exists\": true,\n        \"data_source_exists\": true,\n        \"service_label\": \"service/iam\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"regex_labeler_would_apply\": [\n      \"bug\",\n      \"service/bedrockagentcore\"\n    ],\n    \"primary_service_label\": \"service/bedrockagentcore\"\n  },\n  \"versions\": {\n    \"terraform\": null,\n    \"provider\": null,\n    \"latest_release\": \"6.65.0\",\n    \"latest_release_date\": \"2026-09-16\",\n    \"provider_status\": \"not_reported\",\n    \"newer_release_notes\": [],\n    \"newer_fixes\": []\n  },\n  \"similar_issues\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 49594,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#49594\",\n      \"title\": \"[Bug]: aws_bedrockagentcore_harness: servic